{
  "server": "en",
  "storyId": "act41side_level_act41side_07_beg",
  "groupId": "act41side",
  "stageId": "act41side_07",
  "title": "One Who Burns the Lamp",
  "storyCode": "EA-7",
  "avgTag": "Before Operation",
  "sourcePath": "vendor/ArknightsData/en/gamedata/story/activities/act41side/level_act41side_07_beg.txt",
  "sourceHash": "c927800c00afdf67ec37d3e3f5cfa0258fa5716aba283900d2a23a8b780c726b",
  "bodyAvailable": true,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "'The Leader'",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "How far is County Hillock?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Harmonie",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Far."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "'The Leader'",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "My sister must have known..."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Harmonie",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Only The Elocutionist and his band of idiots would consider this plan flawless."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "'The Leader'",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Then why are you still following me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Harmonie",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Oh, believe me, if it were up to me I'd be taking a nap in camp right about now."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "'The Leader'",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Why didn't my sister stop me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Harmonie",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "I don't know. Maybe she has high hopes for you."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "'The Leader'",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "No, that's impossible. She's never looked at me like that. When I agreed to be her shadow, she..."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "'The Leader'",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Please, Harmonie... tell her I don't want to do this."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Harmonie",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "That you don't want to go to County Hillock?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "'The Leader'",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Mhm. And if she's in a good mood, could you also tell her that, from now on, I'll—"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "'The Leader'",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "'The Leader'",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "No, never mind."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Harmonie",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Fine, can't hurt to pass it along, I suppose. Although it's not easy avoiding The Elocutionist's eyes and ears."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "'The Leader'",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Thank you. You should go..."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "'The Leader'",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "...before she gets bored."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The dead dragon lies on the ground.\nBehind the living dragon, the wayward wakewoman suddenly understands it all."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "She deceived you."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "No, she didn't deceive anyone."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "She set this all up, knowing you would never allow the entire city to die with her!"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "She baited you into piercing her vessel, freeing her from her bonds and allowing the purple fire to spread, burning us all to ashes on the eve of Samhain!"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Why would she take such a risk for a festival that she never cared about?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "I'm affected by the purple flames too. I can feel the flames of death burning in my chest, colder than ever. So cold I'm growing number by the minute!"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "It doesn't matter whether she's seeking dominion over all of Tara, or if she's simply gone mad and wants the city to die with her!"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "It's neither. Tara already belongs to her, and she was very much lucid. She..."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "She—"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Nemos, is her body still there?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "I'll go check."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The wayward wakewoman's brow is furrowed. Perhaps she has never felt such malice in all her life, and as such has never harbored such resolve."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Her body is—"
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The sound of burning drowns out her answer."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Whatever she's trying to do, Na Saoirsí is not fully gone. The fire-returning ceremony can still go on... it <i>must</i> go on."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "I'm well aware."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "I'll inform the citizens that the wicked red dragon they worshipped is dead."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "What about Brigid?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "I've asked her to leave the city and find the wakemen."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "And how are you going to tell people that Eblana is dead?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "With a coffin. That seems appropriate."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Even coffins are in short supply, but she is not some nameless nobody. She deserves one."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Is something wrong?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "No. I'm simply realizing how ugly the path she walked is, a path that even now waves at me invitingly... And it's an invitation I have no choice but to accept."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Go, Nemos. I will buy you some time."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Nemos",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "You mean from the dark mist?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Yes. If it wants to be a part of the Samhain festivities, I will keep it at bay."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Noble Red Dragon",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "I can hardly wait to ask the mist how to return the Red Dragon's flame to darkness."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "'I can hardly wait to ask the mist how to return the Red Dragon's flame to darkness.'"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "How do you feel about that line?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Now, the ending of the dragon and her reflection is clear enough."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The writer stands up with a start."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Who are you and what do you want?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "All I want is to finish the story that you would not."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Didn't you say I was the type who liked to piece together the truth? We've gotten so very close to it."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "This is enough. I'm leaving—"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "If you won't tell the ending yourself, I suppose it falls on me."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "What do you think?"
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "..."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "You've been glancing over there at the newspapers. But not everything reported is a fact."
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The writer looks towards the door.\nHe tries to imagine himself running out of the tavern, but it is such a preposterous proposition that he almost laughs out loud.\nIf not everything reported is a fact, then he finally knows who this woman is, and why she is here.\nHe also knows that there is no escape.\nBut there is something else he realizes.\nPerhaps this is his chance to truly find the ending he had hoped for.\nNo matter who she is, as long as the story continues, they are equals.\nHe feels his spirit return."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Okay. I don't care who you are, or why you're here, but that's no way to tell a story."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "You haven't given it an ending. All you did was extend an ending-less story."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "But I have to know—did you... really see a red dragon kill another?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "In the same sense that you saw the hero drag a giant metal skeleton to the square. A creative liberty, nothing more."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Then take responsibility for it. So the dragon in the mirror accidentally caused her other self to burn to death in the fire. What next? What did the people do? What about the dragon in the mirror?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "What about you? Don't you have any ideas of your own?"
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "For the first time in a long while, the writer takes out a fountain pen from his pocket, then grabs one of the playing cards on the table. He tries to write something, but the tip of the pen has dried out from disuse."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "I need... time."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "But if it can be connected... then maybe..."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Connected?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Let me guess. You're talking about the last story that you published?"
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The writer's pen scratches hard against the card. Finally, some ink oozes out of the tip.\nHe is suddenly reminded of the words of Seamus Williams—'May death connect us with all legends.'\nSeamus Williams is dead. But he himself might—if he may be so impertinent—have a chance to be connected with the legends he wrote.\nHe tries to scribble the poem on the card, but the pen leaves only broken, illegible ink trails."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Just maybe..."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Yes?"
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The writer sits back on the chair, his back even straighter than before.\nHe suddenly feels an urge, the same one he felt after hearing a Seamus Williams poem for the first time.\nThe same feeling that had taken him down this wretched path, which seizes his chest and makes him want to sing, to yell—\nTo create."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "You may have indeed solved a problem for me."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "As I said, what I've seen, what I believe, and what I've said all contradict one another. Thanks to you, though, they are finally beginning to converge."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "How lovely for you."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Now, are you ready to start telling the third story?"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "Of course... of course."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "But I'll need your help."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "You will need to pick up the narrative whenever I get stuck."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "This is my story, but it's also yours."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Writer",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "It has always been yours."
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speakerName": "Mysterious Woman",
      "speakerToken": null,
      "operatorId": null,
      "portraitKey": null,
      "text": "With pleasure."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    },
    {
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The writer's breathing is rapid, his face red. His fountain pen still refuses to write, so he throws it on the table.\nYes. Of course.\nHas he not seen enough of those things already?\nSo what?\nHe is a writer. He will soon find the ending of his story."
    },
    {
      "type": "sceneBreak"
    }
  ],
  "observedOperators": []
}
